                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "df74e3f4-4808-3f91-97d2-ee19868c8d26",
                        "entry_id": "e64e5697-5b7c-3dcd-a9c4-0d82919c6d04",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Tending to talk a lot; fluent or voluble in speech (generally with an unfavourable connotation)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "of a person"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7f434270-aee7-49c2-a51a-e5257e469665",
                                "sense_id": "df74e3f4-4808-3f91-97d2-ee19868c8d26",
                                "text": "1608, Philip Woodward, Bels Trial Examined, Doai, Preface,\nSeeing then he is now so mute, that before was so tonguy […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "042b4999-20a9-4816-958e-d3085d642a47",
                                "sense_id": "df74e3f4-4808-3f91-97d2-ee19868c8d26",
                                "text": "“You air a tongue-y person, Gen’ral. For you talk too much, and that’s a fact,” said Scadder. “You speak a-larmingly well in public, but you didn’t ought to go ahead so fast in private. Now!”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "305aa495-4373-4751-af96-90a369b08cfe",
                                "sense_id": "df74e3f4-4808-3f91-97d2-ee19868c8d26",
                                "text": "“[…] He had many friends who loved him truly and they tried to persuade him to escape, but by unanswerable arguments he proved to them how wrong they were.” ¶ “Humph!” grunted Sallie. “Tonguey to de last! An’ in de wrong way to de wrong ones.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8fdf4e7e-12a0-3921-8e31-748abf68bead",
                        "entry_id": "e64e5697-5b7c-3dcd-a9c4-0d82919c6d04",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Using many words; containing grandiloquent expressions; marked by rhetorical elegance (generally with an unfavourable connotation)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "of speech"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c764e43b-b32d-4fa1-8b69-56582385f4ea",
                                "sense_id": "8fdf4e7e-12a0-3921-8e31-748abf68bead",
                                "text": "1885, J. H. Battle, Kentucky: A History of the State, Louisville, KY: F.A. Battey, “Biographical Sketches,” p. 839,\n[…] personal abuse and tonguy sarcasm are not elements of success in law practice."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8277cd91-be99-46a8-89a3-85b54b5d3272",
                                "sense_id": "8fdf4e7e-12a0-3921-8e31-748abf68bead",
                                "text": "“I have listened,” he said, “to the talk that Justice Rowan has given us. It’s very fine and tonguey, but it smothers up the facts. […]”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "85b05744-a878-4358-9887-beec2ce69f8b",
                                "sense_id": "8fdf4e7e-12a0-3921-8e31-748abf68bead",
                                "text": "those points especially warming to tonguey gossip—the neighboring tavern and country-store"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "070d8e1c-35ca-3d5e-b740-51a9390a2093",
                        "entry_id": "e64e5697-5b7c-3dcd-a9c4-0d82919c6d04",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Manifested by fluent or voluble speech."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "of a quality"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "139ab247-7b60-4d45-83ec-b9663da912c9",
                                "sense_id": "070d8e1c-35ca-3d5e-b740-51a9390a2093",
                                "text": "[…] even his tonguey confidence and ingenuousness could glean but little satisfaction from his interviews with the rheumatic and unbelieving old woman."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a70e6f2a-c561-3ee4-9873-9c3697891e62",
                        "entry_id": "e64e5697-5b7c-3dcd-a9c4-0d82919c6d04",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Involving the tongue."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "733e0d29-befd-45f6-ab72-fdb993d4735b",
                                "sense_id": "a70e6f2a-c561-3ee4-9873-9c3697891e62",
                                "text": "Wully seated himself upon the corner of the kitchen table, from beneath which appeared a dog’s welcoming nose accompanied by a tonguey, tooth-trimmed grin."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e07db5bf-37db-4961-ae14-cea48bad6f61",
                                "sense_id": "a70e6f2a-c561-3ee4-9873-9c3697891e62",
                                "text": "They take each other’s hands and kiss goodbye, a longish tonguey kiss […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "94d799eb-9263-3951-a0ad-035da027a02d",
                        "entry_id": "e64e5697-5b7c-3dcd-a9c4-0d82919c6d04",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Resembling a tongue."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7b23be98-27ad-40eb-bce1-afe5dcaf5818",
                                "sense_id": "94d799eb-9263-3951-a0ad-035da027a02d",
                                "text": "1882, Albert Kellogg, Forest Trees of California, Sacramento: J.D. Young, “The Noble Silver Fir,” p. 34,\nThese tonguey bracts or scaly appendages […] never become shorter than the proper cone scales, or so as to be hid from outside view."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "908eccd5-0d57-44ef-8589-cfdbbbd077b9",
                                "sense_id": "94d799eb-9263-3951-a0ad-035da027a02d",
                                "text": "[…] the brain-aura […] crowns the head after the manner of the tonguey flames of a torch."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c18c9ae0-749d-45d5-872c-06deac4e877b",
                                "sense_id": "94d799eb-9263-3951-a0ad-035da027a02d",
                                "text": "Fleur leans back against the kitchen table, letting her face be licked by the tonguey vapour of her coffee-cup."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
